{* The activity indicator over the whole page while it waits on the server, on every page and shown
	by javascript/busy.js. Here rather than built by the script, and its icon preloaded
	(Icon::preload()), so it is drawn the moment it is needed: a page that has started navigating
	away loads nothing more. Stop comes in once the wait has taken a while (css/busy.css): a server
	that never answers would otherwise keep the page turning until the connection times out. *}
<div id="ad-busy" popover="manual"><span role="progressbar" aria-label="{t('busy.loading')}">{\Desktop\Assets\Icon::Spinner->html()|noescape}</span><button type="button" class="ad-busy-stop">{t('busy.stop')}</button></div>
